  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "template_sanity_check",
    "file": "opensc/src/pkcs15init/profile.c",
    "description": "`template_sanity_check` validates only that each copied `sc_path.len` is at least 2, but never verifies that it is at most `sizeof(sc_path.value)` (`SC_MAX_PATH_SIZE`). It then indexes `ffi_path.value[ffi_path.len - 2]` and `[ffi_path.len - 1]` (likewise for `fi_path`). With an inconsistent oversized length, these accesses run beyond the local `sc_path` copy; in this PoV they land in a returned stack frame and ASan reports stack-use-after-return at line 1094. The sanity check must reject path lengths outside `[2, sizeof(path.value)]` before either index.",
    "conditions": "The fuzz input is parsed as a PKCS#15 profile and reaches a `filesystem` template containing file entries. A malformed/inconsistent file path state with `path.len > SC_MAX_PATH_SIZE` is retained in the template's `ef_list`; `process_tmpl` completes `process_block` successfully and invokes `template_sanity_check`. During its nested comparison of template files, the oversized `ffi->file->path.len` is copied and used as an unchecked array index, producing the out-of-bounds stack read. The supplied malformed, deeply nested/repeated template profile triggers this state and the read."
  },
